lly  depends on the autoimmune disease that  the woman has prior to the pregnancy so  a woman with rheumatoid arthritis or  multiple sclerosis will actually show  improvements in their disease  so particularly in the third trimester  of pregnancy a woman with relapsing  remitting multiple sclerosis for example  would show fewer relapses compared to  her own relapse rates prior to the  pregnancy and then she will often crash  into a relapse in the first few months  after the baby is born and the same with  women with rheumatoid arthritis they'll  have fewer flares during the pregnancy  whereas a woman who's got systemic lupus  arithmetosis will actually get worsening  disease so it really depends on what her  autoimmune disease but again we do see  that pregnancy has quite a profound  effect on that autoimmune disease  profile probably driven by those immune  plasticity changes that are occurring in  the pregnant woman  thank you so much now you showed a  solution for untouched  pbmc isolation  is it possible to do further magnetic  isolations after the pbmc isolation kit  you can take this one um yes so the  isolation is completely untouched so  your pvmcs are have no microbeads on  them so you can then  use any of the kits i showed before to  isolate further uh cells that you might  be interested in so you could  isolate only monocytes but t cells b  cells whatever you are interested in  thank you very much salvador and i want  to thank our audience for these great  questions coming in  do these  um how long does the immune system take  to go back to basil levels after  pregnancy  well i think the the short answer is  nobody actually knows because not a lot  of people actually a lot of studies in  pregnancy and a lot of studies in the  second and third trimester of pregnancy  but not a lot of studies on those immune  changes that may be occurring very early  on from just before the conception  through the first trimester and then not  very many after the pregnancy 